---
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Python Random Scripts';
const pageDescription = 'A portfolio snapshot highlighting a grab bag of automation and scripting experiments in Python.';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/lefos13/python-random-scripts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main class="page">
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Project Spotlight</p>
        <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A living collection of small Python utilities where I explore everyday automation, quick data
          experiments, and CLI helpers. Each script solves a specific problem and doubles as a playground for
          sharpening language features and third-party packages.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content">
        <h2>What Lives in the Repo</h2>
        <p>
          The repository is intentionally eclectic: batch file renamers, API data fetchers, CSV cleaners, and
          shell-friendly tooling. It is where ideas start lightweight before they grow into standalone
          services or libraries.
        </p>

        <h3>Highlights</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Hands-on automation scripts for file management, notifications, and workflow shortcuts.</li>
          <li>Data wrangling helpers that tidy CSV and JSON payloads with pandas and native tooling.</li>
          <li>Command-line experiments that showcase argparse patterns, logging, and packaging basics.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Why It Matters</h3>
        <p>
          Keeping a sandbox like this lets me iterate quickly, try new libraries, and carry working patterns
          into production projects. It also gives collaborators tangible, copy-ready snippets for their own
          use cases.
        </p>

        <p class="cta">
          Browse the scripts, star the repository, or open an issue with your own automation idea:
          <a href={repoUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{repoUrl}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .page {
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 960px;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  .hero {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent, #4b63ff);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }

  .content h2,
  .content h3 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .content ul {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .cta {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent, #4b63ff);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
</style>
